1588-    {
1589:      "id": "phase-068",
1590-      "title": "Talk to the shell without leaving: `!cmd`, `.pipe`, `.cd`, `.pwd`, `.ls`",
1591-      "severity": "major",
1592-      "depends_on": [
1593-        "phase-067"
1594-      ],
1595-      "risk": "medium",
1596-      "finding": "The session is sealed from its own machine: `pipe`, `cd`, `pwd` and `ls` are all absent from commands.rs (verified), and no `!` shell escape exists — so running a file listing, checking a path, or sending output through a pager means suspending the REPL and opening a second terminal. Ipp ships `! <cmd>` (shell execute), `.pipe <cmd>` (output to shell), and `.cd`/`.ls`/`.pwd` (navigation) as REPL-native because file arguments (`:load`, `:save`, `:export`) are typed blind without them — which phase-060's path completion only half fixes: completion needs a visible directory.",
1597-      "goal": "Add `!cmd` (run a shell command, show its output and exit code), `.pipe <cmd>` (send the last result/output through a shell command), and `.cd`/`.pwd`/`.ls` (session working directory affecting all relative file arguments). Shell features are host-only and labeled as such; on targets without a shell they refuse cleanly rather than failing obscurely.",
1598-      "must_touch": [
1599-        "src/"
1600-      ],
1601-      "accept": [
1602-        "`!echo hi` prints `hi` and a zero exit (asserted on both, so a silent failure cannot pass); a failing command prints its exit code rather than the REPL's error format",
1603-        "`.pipe` sends the last `_` value to the command's stdin (pinned with a stdin-echo command, proving the direction); with no last result it says so instead of piping emptiness",
1604-        "`.cd` into a temp dir makes `:load` resolve there (proved by loading a file by bare name after `.cd`), and `.pwd` prints the session directory distinctly from the process directory",
1605-        "`.ls` lists the session directory with directories marked (trailing separator, matching the phase-060 completion contract so the two agree)",
1606-        "edge_* tests cover `!` with an empty command (usage, no shell spawned), `.pipe` to a command that fails (exit code surfaces, session survives), `.cd` to a missing directory (clean error naming the path, directory unchanged), and a 1MB piped payload (streams, never loads whole into a string twice)"
1607-      ],
1608-      "timeout_min": 120
1609-    },
1610-    {
1611-      "id": "phase-069",
1612-      "title": "Find things without leaving: `.search` across docs, history, bindings and help",
1613-      "severity": "major",
1614-      "depends_on": [
1615:        "phase-068"
1616-      ],
1617-      "risk": "medium",
1618-      "finding": "`search` is absent from commands.rs (verified), so every lookup is a different tool: builtin docs need `.doc` with the exact name, history needs eyeballing `:history`, session bindings need eyeballing `:vars`, and help needs reading end to end. `which builtin does string splitting` has no answer inside the session although the data is all there — the registry, the help table, the history buffer and the session map. Ipp's `.search <kw>` searches builtin documentation in one place for exactly this reason.",
1619-      "goal": "Add `.search <keyword>` ranking matches across four sources — builtin docs/signatures, `:help` text, session bindings, and history — with the source labeled per hit. Read-only: searching never executes, binds, or reorders anything.",
1620-      "must_touch": [
1621-        "src/"
1622-      ],
1623-      "accept": [
1624-        "`.search split` finds the `split` builtin, the phase-056 `.sighelp` entry if present, and any history line mentioning it, each labeled with its source (asserted per-source, so a source going dark fails the test)",
1625-        "`.search` ranks exact-name matches above substring matches (pinned on a fixed query with both kinds present)",
1626-        "`.search` with no argument prints usage rather than dumping every source (a full dump is a denial-of-patience, not a search)",
1627-        "history matches show their history numbers so the hit can be re-run with `!!`-style recall or by number",
1628-        "edge_* tests cover a keyword matching nothing (named empty per source, never a blank page), a 1-character keyword (refused as too short with the minimum stated, so single letters never dump the registry), and regex-significant characters in the keyword (treated literally, never as a pattern)"
1629-      ],
1630-      "timeout_min": 120
1631-    },
